  "term": "n-Ach",
  "definition": "N. Ach refers to a historical psychologist cited in discussions of systematic experimental introspection, especially work on will, thought, and the careful reporting of conscious experience. In this context, Ach is associated with stressing complete description, caution about suggestive questioning, and the need to check introspective reports by varying experimental conditions.",
